  "description": "The Black Adder is the highlight among BULLS' cross-country hardtails. With its highly developed carbon frame and outstanding equipment, the off-road racer offers minimum weight and maximum performance. As the centrepiece of the Endurance Lite Concept, the frame in size M weighs just 900 grams. But in addition to its low weight, its carbon fibre lay-up developed with Team BULLS is particularly impressive. This achieves full performance and control in the drive and control-relevant areas. At the same time, a different fibre mix in the seat tube area ensures maximum sporty comfort for full performance over long distances. The geometry has been fine-tuned once again in close consultation with the professionals from Team BULLS. The top tube is slightly longer, the chainstays slightly shorter and the head tube angle 0.5 degrees slacker - small changes to further improve the riding behaviour. With Shimano Deore 12-speed gears, RockShox Reba suspension fork, carbon seatpost and a high-quality Schwalbe tyre mix, the Black Adder is ideally equipped for training and racing off-road.",
